Assignment Title: The Sci-Fi Film Poster Challenge
Prompt: Create a promotional science-fiction poster for an upcoming film set on a remote, abandoned ocean planet inspired by the vast flooded landscapes of Miller’s planet. The setting features an endless reflective sea stretching to the horizon beneath a dramatic orange-pink sunset. The sky will have clusters of futuristic modern glass townhouses with lights shining out the windows creating vertical lines in the sky and into the ocean below. The ocean will have natural irregular horizontal lines formed by the horizon and waves throughout the water. The poster should be dominated by rectangular geometric shapes in the glass townhouses, contrasted by the curvy organic shape formed by the ocean, clouds, and sun. The floating buildings will be the positive space in the upper half of the design, while the expansive sky and endless ocean will be the negative space; the vastness of negative space from the ocean will make the planet feel lonely and abandoned. The surface of the townhouses will be sleek transparent glass, polished metallic supports, and reflective windows that contrast the rippling texture of the waves within the ocean dancing with each other. The focal point will be one central floating townhouse directly in front of the sunset with the bright golden sun illuminating the glass of that lone townhouse making it brighter than the other townhouses while the others are slightly dimmer in color.
